{"conversation":"Okay, so I need to keep track of characters in the current substring. Maybe I can use a set to store characters as I scan through the string. When I find a repeated character, I start a new substring and reset the set. I'll try to code this idea.","python_code":"class Solution:
    def partitionString(self, s: str) -> int:
        seen = set()
        count = 1
        for char in s:
            if char in seen:
                count += 1
                seen = set()
            seen.add(char)
        return count"}
